      {
        "slide": 9,
        "role": "close",
        "subject": "A survey quadcopter at rest on a plum rubber launch mat with H markings and a ring. Its shell is open with the flight board showing, its four props are unfolded and still, and nothing is lit. Beside it sits an open lavender hard case of 21 labelled cartridges, with a 22nd standing on the mat by the drone's legs. They rest on a straw and apricot bluestem crest at last light above a plum valley, with oak mottes, a far ridge with a saddle and pale cattle trails",
        "visual_consequence": "The deck returns to frame 1's ridge with the drone grounded, opened up and still, and the held-back records beside it, one taken out. The new closing sentence asks how a drone might estimate its location without reliable information, and that suits a grounded, opened machine with no glow. At 432 px the drone, mat and case fill the middle of the frame and read, and no amber appears",
        "weakness": "The picture is unchanged from the fourth reading. The dek now runs five lines and ends about 40 px above the far ridge line, legible on the plum seat with a tighter margin. The mat's long cast shadow has ruler-straight edges, the near clay is a blurred smear, the oak crowns carry speckle and the open case lid is a flat panel. The drone, mat, cartridges and case are finished",
        "repair": "Soften and break up the mat's long cast shadow with contact hardening on displaced soil, and add fine grain detail to the near clay",
